y":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"**I'm submitting a ...** \n\n```\n[x] bug report\n[ ] feature request\n```\n\n**Current behavior**\n\nSpecifying an easing in the animate() function has no effect on the animation.\n\ni.e. These all animate the same visually\n\n``` typescript\ntransition(\"* => void\", [\n   animate(\"1s\", style({\n      transform: \"translateX( 100% )\"\n   }))\n])\ntransition(\"* => void\", [\n   animate(\"1s ease-in\", style({\n      transform: \"translateX( 100% )\"\n   }))\n])\ntransition(\"* => void\", [\n   animate(\"1s cubic-bezier(0.6, -0.28, 0.735, 0.045)\", style({\n      transform: \"translateX( 100% )\"\n   }))\n])\n```\n\n**Expected/desired behavior**\n\nI expect the specified easing function to change the visual appearance/timing of the animation.\n\n**Reproduction of the problem**\n\n[See this plunker](http://plnkr.co/edit/QR6WDzv6NxOmn6LXTngG?p=preview)\n\n**What is the expected behavior?**\n\nIn the plunker, all 3 animations play exactly the same currently. I expect the 3 to be different (unless the default easing is one of the above when not specified)\n\n**What is the motivation / use case for changing the behavior?**\n\nShould work as advertised in the docs. (I haven't attempted keyframes yet... as easing should suffice)\n\n**Please tell us about your environment:**\n- **Angular version:** 2.0.0-rc.3\n- **Browser:** Chrome 51.0.2704.84 m\n- **Language:** TypeScript 1.9.0-dev.20160409, plugin-typescript@4.0.10  (see plunker)\n\ncc @matsko \n","closed_by":{"login":"matsko","id":93018,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkzMDE4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/93018?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/matsko","html_url":"https://github.com/matsko","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matsko/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matsko/following{/other_us